    "All six tasks passed tool evidence and state verification. Each surface used one distinct MCP operation for ticket reading and four for rollback from the 2000-operation catalog.",
    "Native used less accumulated input than CLI and hybrid in this small follow-up. CLI provider-reported effective cost was about 3.7% lower than native despite about 1.60x accumulated input; this run does not establish a universal cheapest surface.",
    "Cache-read counts are observational. This MCP run overlapped the frozen platform comparison; no causal cache savings or stable surface ranking is inferred.",
    "Two tasks per surface and one trial per task/surface are a smoke check, not an accuracy or cost benchmark.",
    "10000-tool results are offline retrieval/index stress only. No successful live model accuracy qualification at 10000 tools is claimed.",
    "Stress timings are local dev-profile microbenchmarks and exclude model latency and MCP process/network startup. Serialized bytes are not index heap allocation.",
    "The final offline stress run overlapped a Framework rebuild and platform model checks on the shared executor. CPU contention makes these timings observational rather than a controlled comparison with earlier runs; higher final timings do not establish an algorithmic regression."
